> On 31 July 2006, Jove wrote:
>> On 30 Jul 2006 16:10:12 -0700, azgor wrote:
>>>4: Shuriken shouldn't disappear. They're solid metal, like daggers,
>>>they shouldn't disappear. And then they'd be a somewhat viable weapon
>>>without being enchanted up.
>>
>>   This makes perfect sense.  It's just not that helpful because there's
>> no guaranteed way to get shuriken short of wishing.
>
> Which is precisely why they shouldn't disappear.  Currently, the fact
> that they do disappear makes that skill all but worthless to #enhance,
> because you can never be certain that you'll get enough to replace them.
> Having a poisonable missile that doesn't disappear could in fact be
> worthwhile enough to #enhance for certain classes, if you find some.

It's true, the combination of only being generated randomly and
disappearing makes shuriken uninteresting. But the fact that only
disappearing missile weapons are poisonable was a deliberate decision by
the devteam for balance reasons. If shuriken are made permanent and still
poisonable as a reasonable (see above) exception, there can never be a
guaranteed source of shuriken introduced into the game in the future. So
either leave everything as it is now, or make them permanent _and_
non-poisonable.

> Particularly given that they are so much lighter than daggers.  As it
> is, they're just expensive darts, in a different class.  (The extra
> damage is offset by the ability to enchant hundreds of darts at once.)

Hundreds, dozens, with non-disappearing missiles, there's no practical
difference. So permanent non-poisonable shuriken would have a rightful
place among the other missiles.


